    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers entirely.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` per-city sequence) with `customerCodeFor(owner)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - **REGION** = region code derived from the postcode (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, or `UNKNOWN` when the postcode is absent or in no known range), via the mapper's existing `regionFromPostcode`.\n  - **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars (first 4 bytes) of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, computed by a new `hash8` helper. The telephone is already normalized to E.164 at the point the code is built.\n- Updated the `addOwner` call site to `owner.setCustomerCode(customerCodeFor(owner))`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Redefined `locality(owner)` to derive from the new identity: it returns the `<REGION>` segment of the `customerCode`, falling back to the postcode/city derivation only for legacy records with no valid code.\n\nEverything else built from `customerCode` \u2014 the `membershipNumber`, its Luhn `checkDigit`, and the create audit line \u2014 reads the field directly, so they automatically move to the new region-and-hash identity (the test run logged `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite pass.",
